</span></pre></td></tr></tbody></table></code></pre></div></div>

<h3 id="seconds-in-a-year">Seconds in a year</h3>

<p>For a year, we usually assume it has 365 days, except in leap years, when it has 366 days. Therefore, the total seconds in a year can be calculated as:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Non-leap year:
[ \text{total seconds in a year} = 365 \times 24 \times 60 \times 60 ]</li>
  <li>Leap year:
[ \text{total seconds in a year} = 366 \times 24 \times 60 \times 60 ]</li>
</ul>

<p>Non-leap year: <br />
Total seconds in a year = 365 × 24 × 60 × 60<br />
Leap year: <br />
Total seconds in a year = 366 × 24 × 60 × 60</p>

<p>The results are approximately:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Non-leap year: 31,536,000 seconds</li>
  <li>Leap year: 31,622,400 seconds</li>
</ul>

